Verse 1:
[D]I hear the Savior say, "Thy [A]strength indeed is [D]small;
[D]Child of weakness, watch and pray, Find in [A]Me thine all in [D]all."
[D]Jesus paid it all, All to Him I [A]owe;
[D]Sin had left a crimson [G]stain, [E7]He [A]washed it white as [D]snow.

Refrain:
[D]Jesus [A]paid [D]it all,
[D]All [A]to Him [D]I owe;
[D]Sin had left [A]a crimson stain,
[D]He [G]washed [E7]it [A]white [D]as snow.

Verse 2:
[D]Lord, [A]now indeed [D]I find
[D]Thy [A]power and [D]Thine alone,
[D]Can change [A]the leper's spots
[D]And [G]melt [E7]the [A]heart [D]of stone.

Verse 3:
[D]Since [A]nothing good [D]have I
[D]Whereby [A]Thy grace [D]to claim,
[D]I'll wash [A]my garments white
[D]In [G]the [E7]blood [A]of [D]Calv'ry's Lamb.

Verse 4:
[D]And [A]when before [D]the throne
[D]I [A]stand in [D]Him complete,
[D]I'll lay [A]my trophies down
[D]All [G]down [E7]at [A]Jesus' [D]feet.
